      "speaker": "Giacomo Cordoni",
      "title": "Bridging Stellar and Galactic Evolution through Star Clusters",
      "abstract": "Star clusters are fundamental laboratories for stellar astrophysics, linking the evolution of individual stars to the formation history of the Milky Way. Despite decades of study, key stages in their life cycle — from the early impact of stellar rotation in young clusters to the complex chemical signatures in ancient globulars — remain poorly understood. In this talk, I will outline my past and ongoing work on cluster dynamics, stellar rotation, and multiple populations, and present the goals of my Ambizione project. By tracing how clusters form, evolve, and dissolve, this research aims to connect stellar evolution with Galactic archaeology and provide new insights into the Milky Way’s history."
