      "title": "Modelling the rotational evolution of solar-like stars",
      "abstract": "Between its formation stage as an actively accreting seed and today, the Sun underwent large structural changes as well as variation in magnetic activity, rotation rate and its relation to the surrounding environment.  In this talk, I will go through the different processes that are responsible for these changes and present my contribution to the topic.  I will discuss the early interaction between the star and its proto-planetary disc, followed by the evolution on the main sequence and what we can obtain from comparing models with photometric and spectroscopic surveys, to end on the way evolved stars are still able to generate a magnetic field despite their very slow rotation rate."
