      "abstract": "In this talk, I will give an overview of some studies I carried out during my time at the observatory. I will start with the curation of a historical catalogue with all young stellar objects (YSOs) ever studied in the Orion star formation complex, which I built with the goal of training and validating machine learning applications focused on young stars. Then I will show some examples of this catalogue in use within our NEMESIS project, including a YSO classifier used to identify 300,000 YSOs all-sky. Then I will talk about classifying YSOs according to their variability with Gaia. And finally, I will tell what this all has to do with wine, which will be the theme of my research starting in November."
