      "time": "10:00",
      "place": "Astrotech Jura",
      "speaker": "Thomas Voje",
      "title": "Realistic atmospheres in massive stellar evolution models",
      "abstract": "Realistic model atmospheres have progressively been included through various methods in state-of-the-art low- and intermediate-mass stars evolution calculations. At the same time model atmospheres for massive stars have become increasingly more realistic over the last 50 years, with the progressive inclusion of non-LTE and non-gray effects, wind extension, and line-blanketing. However all these improvements have never been included in massive star evolution calculations, which in their vast majority still use the Eddington gray approximation. In this talk I will present two different methods we developed to include realistic model atmospheres in the evolution calculations of massive stars, along with applications of these methods to the evolution of a 60 solar mass star at solar metallicity."
