      "speaker": "André Oliva",
      "title": "Jets and rotating massive protostars",
      "abstract": "During the formation of massive stars, accretion disks and protostellar jets are formed, which are of magnetic origin. Using magnetohydrodynamical simulations with the PLUTO code (and additional modules for radiation transport and self-gravity), we have been able to model the angular momentum removal of the jets from the inner disk, and extended our models to include the angular momentum removed from the protostellar surface. Using this approach, we are able to build pre-main sequence evolution models of rotating and accreting massive protostars using Genec without reaching the critical rotation rate. Our results show that the ratio of the surface rotation rate to the critical rotation rate depends on the jet strength, which itself depends on the conditions of the parent molecular cloud. Additionally, I will give a tour of ongoing projects in the newly established 'Beiwa' research group at the University of Costa Rica."
